# Makefile Workflow for Cursor

Follow these steps in order for every coding task:

1. Make sure that `git status --short` is clean, then create branch `feat/<id>-<slug>` or `fix/<id>-<slug>` (use `feat/local-<n>-<slug>` for local tasks).
2. Scan the repository to detect subprojects and test runners. If no tests exist, create a smoke test first.
3. Present an implementation plan in chat. If existing tests must change, explain why and wait for user approval.
4. Write failing unit tests first. Point tests to isolated test databases, configured `database.testDatabases`, or mocks, never production data. Before Target 40 review, run the full active subproject regression suite (`verify-regression`) to seal `.workflow/state/30_regression_receipt.json`. Keep `review.allowCriticHermeticTests` set to `false` by default.
5. Audit your diff against the Six Pillars: Intent, Verification (TDD, failure falsification, boundary limits), Architecture (including Gang of Four, Game Programming Patterns, and ORM versus parameterized query balance), Blast Radius (mandatory canary), Reviewer Defense (intentional non-changes, Simple English), and Immune Defenses & Crash Antibodies.
6. Run formatters, linters, and the full test suite across all subprojects before you ask to commit.
7. Stop and wait for explicit human approval at all six pause gates: Target 20 (plan), Target 42 (blocker triage), Target 45 (review), Target 50 (commit), Target 60 (push), and Target 75 (landing). Never declare or approve gates yourself under SCAR-PROC-102. Forbid agent self-approval. Forbid `closes #` on local session commits.
8. Write documentation and pull request summaries in Simple English with short sentences and active voice.
9. Read cascaded config from `~/.cursor/plugin_data/makeflow/config.json` (or legacy `~/.gemini/config/makeflow.json`) and `.workflow/config.json` when present. Store user-wide scars in `~/.cursor/plugin_data/makeflow/scars/` alongside `.workflow/scars/` and configured `scars.directories`.
10. Intercept POSIX signals (`SIGTERM` and `SIGINT`) in long-running workers and clean up lockfiles under `SCAR-SYS-07`.
11. If shell commands require complex string escaping or multiple quoting layers, write the script to a file in a temporary directory. Pass the path to the runtime interpreter under `SCAR-SH-01`.
12. Encapsulate script logic in testable classes using the BaseScript Template Method pattern under `SCAR-ARCH-05`. Separate library modules in `lib/` without shebangs, thin CLI wrappers in `scripts/`, and unit tests in `tests/`. Enforce polyglot layer separation (`entrypoints -> library`) and Target 20 structural debt triage under `SCAR-ARCH-08`.
13. Use atomic directory creation (`mkdir`) for mutual exclusion locks under `SCAR-SYS-08`.
14. Never arbitrarily impose `--limit` or truncation flags before assessing the full dataset. If output volume threatens context limits, halt tool execution immediately. Interview the user to select a triage path under `SCAR-TOOL-16`.
15. Enforce Immediate Supervisory Halt (`tool_calls: []`) while phase subagents run (`SCAR-PROC-95`). Defer live bug reproduction to Target 30 instead of Target 15.
16. At Target 15, capture the Git file tree index with `make -f .workflow/state/Makefile repo-tree` under `SCAR-TOOL-16` triage before dispatching archaeology. Attach that index in the prompt, or call `workflow_repo_tree` as the read-only MCP fallback.
17. After Target 40 review, write `.workflow/state/40_critic_review_round<N>.md` once. Run `make -f .workflow/state/Makefile promote-review ROUND=<N>` to promote `.workflow/state/40_critic_review.md`. At Target 45, write 1 to 2 concise sentences per pillar heading with a `file://` link to `.workflow/state/40_critic_review.md`. Present Target 42 and Target 45 proposals and NBO options in plain chat. Stop tool calls (`tool_calls: []`), and never call `ask_question`.
18. Treat the Makeflow harness as a black box during Target 30 through Target 90 (`SCAR-PROC-124`). Do not read out-of-scope guard scripts or `.workflow/state/gate_entry.json`. Run `make -f .workflow/state/Makefile` targets directly and follow any Vector 4 Reflex on exit code `2`.
19. Persist structured subagent reports as canonical `.json` with rendered `.md` views via MCP `workflow_submit_report` (`SCAR-ARCH-10`, `SCAR-TOOL-13`).

## Model Switch Reminder

If `.workflow/config.json` specifies models or "inherit", bypass the model picker prompt. When unconfigured, prompt the user in chat when entering and leaving the review gate:

1. At Target 40, prompt the user: "Switch the model picker to a deep-reasoning model for the Six-Pillar review." Pause (stop tool calls) before dispatching the review.
2. At Target 45, tell the user: "Review passed. You can switch back to your fast coding model."
